id: pm-fl3phm
title: "GH-1520: reject unknown SDK mutation option keys before any write"
description: "GitHub https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1520 reports that JavaScript callers and injected extension clients silently lose misspelled create/update fields. Existing pm-x29o compile-time contracts remain completed; this scope adds runtime admission before normalization can discard input."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: agent-ux,"area:sdk",mutation-safety
created_at: "2026-10-20T11:28:58.471Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T12:55:03.532Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#195da4edbf99e3a7d3dcd1aa"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Native PmClient create/update and run paths reject unknown option keys and misplaced mutation fields with typed usage diagnostics and nearest valid names before item or history writes. Preserve supported top-level aliases, runtime schema fields, injected extension clients, MCP transport contracts and valid typed calls. Prove refusal byte stability and real accepted mutations through public SDK integration tests."
goal: Preserve requested context when JavaScript callers and packages mutate tracker data.
objective: "Reject unknown native mutation keys before dispatch, using executable contracts and active schema identities."
value: Package bugs and misspellings produce actionable refusals instead of silent field loss or partial updates.
why_now: GH-1520 demonstrates successful SDK calls that silently drop requested mutation fields despite the existing compile-time option types.
parent: pm-33cw
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: Mutation typos cannot silently drop data or partially apply a valid subset; callers get actionable no-change refusals.
