comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T11:28:58.471Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: canonical cold start, request-specific search, open and in-progress lists, complete strict 3025-item all-status corpus with no omissions, full pm-x29o and pm-gh1440 lineage reads. No open runtime option-key admission owner found. Reuse completed compile-time owner as related context; implement with pm-hdvxqg as one admission-safety PR."
  "2026-10-20T11:29:19.627Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: validate raw create/update option keys before normalization drops unknown values, including active extension client dispatch and misplaced run arguments. Shared PR with pm-hdvxqg; preserve runtime schema customization and known transport aliases."
  "2026-10-20T11:36:19.218Z","harness:codex","Regression proof: native SDK typo mutation resolved successfully before the change. Runtime client admission now rejects unknown and misplaced create/update keys, preserves schema option identities and existing top-level aliases, and supplies actionable typed no-change context. The same test exercises the active-extension-host client route. Source and installed-candidate verification remain pending."
  "2026-10-20T11:51:49.106Z","harness:codex","Operational evidence: current package audit and GitHub security inventories are clean. Fresh consented get/list probes appear as pm.command spans with command names, timestamps and durations in the Sentry spans dataset; the legacy transaction trace-list endpoint returns no rows for streaming spans. Telemetry storage shows fresh paired sessions and flush drains the logical and physical client queue; broker ready/unacknowledged counts are zero. These are bounded recent-probe observations, not a claim that all historical telemetry is complete."
  "2026-10-20T12:05:34.038Z","harness:codex","The first full-suite pass exposed three validator compatibility gaps: clear flags, structured JSON transport, and the legacy fullChangedFields option. Admission now combines complete per-command flag contracts with registration aliases and explicit projection controls, retaining live schema identities. All seven recovery targets pass together:155 tests, including the strict clear-collection flow, real CLI/SDK custom-field transport, full client API flow, packed Node/Bun continuation, and both unchanged timing controls. The local npm module lookup is resolved with the existing NODE_PATH mechanism; no source threshold or assertion was weakened. A fresh canonical full coverage run is underway with eight workers."
  "2026-10-20T12:49:55.130Z","harness:codex","Additional raw-key negative control: a JSON object containing an own __proto__ option is normalized away and the current guard returns a successful no-op. The owned sandbox probe and the new integration case both reproduce this before the final fix. Admission now checks raw and normalized key sets, so normalization cannot hide an unrecognized input name. The validation module is imported only inside native create/update dispatch, preserving read-path loading discipline. Prior qualified get-budget failure is recorded under the existing runner owner; revised acceptance remains pending."
  "2026-10-20T12:55:03.532Z","harness:codex","Final raw-key focus passes4 files and188 tests, including complete client API flows, declared-schema CLI/SDK roundtrips and both no-change error projections. TypeScript and focused ESLint pass. The fresh isolated npm and Bun candidate probes each refuse4 requests without item/history changes, then execute1 valid linked command; npx and bunx dispatch both succeed. These are installed candidate receipts, distinct from immutable public2026.10.20 release acceptance."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T11:46:46.468Z","harness:codex","Compile-time option types do not protect JavaScript or dynamically constructed package payloads. Validate native raw keys against the executable contract and active schema before dispatch, retaining explicit transport aliases and distinct MCP admission."
